{"w":2400,"lines":[{"c":1,"w":0.078860314687093092,"t":"Reading","x":0.79183528823872207,"y":0.099724038618681843,"h":0.014650275204572072},{"t":"Here is how some of today's 'explorers' define the word. Ran Fiennes, dubbed the 'greatest","y":0.14244186030424477,"w":0.72633743286132812,"h":0.017452132715914948,"x":0.088477374040441634,"c":1},{"t":"living explorer said, 'An explorer is someone who has done something that no human has done","w":0.76954732259114589,"c":1,"h":0.017441860778592888,"y":0.15988372077061608,"x":0.086419754253327596},{"h":0.016046580212416783,"y":0.17726737341736754,"c":1,"x":0.088477367402010329,"t":"before - and also done something scientifically useful. Chris Bonington, a leading mountaineer,","w":0.76954732259114589},{"w":0.73261581420898436,"y":0.19307096069096108,"h":0.017417938043708947,"t":"telt exploration was to be found in the act of physically touching the unknown:iạiYou have to","c":1,"x":0.08842339590048634},{"x":0.088477362970288784,"y":0.2093023254302474,"h":0.015988372380376759,"w":0.74279836018880208,"t":"have gone somewhere new? Then Robin Hanbury-Tenison, a campaigner on behalf of remote","c":1},{"x":0.088411644564072661,"t":"so-called 'tribal' peoples, said, 'A traveller simply records information about some far-off world,","w":0.76556518554687492,"c":1,"h":0.020601313021494705,"y":0.22498098784077414},{"y":0.24411071843758458,"x":0.088477354851531992,"w":0.74074076334635419,"t":"and reports back; but an explorer changes the world.' Wilfred Thesiger, who crossed Arabia's","h":0.0175171886933847,"c":1},{"t":"Empty Quarter in 1946, and belongs to an era of unmechanised travel now lost to the rest of us,","x":0.088477360289773793,"h":0.016032884483202614,"y":0.26017441845629941,"c":1,"w":0.76131688435872391},{"w":0.76768809000651028,"x":0.088409278754995838,"y":0.27466892874739279,"h":0.01961377147229737,"c":1,"t":"told me, 'If I'd gone across by camel when I could have gone by car, it would have been a stunt.?"},{"t":"To him, exploration meant bringing back information from a remote place regardless of any great","x":0.088429671913954927,"w":0.77993250528971358,"h":0.018754727708436891,"c":1,"y":0.29242785675891525},{"h":0.014633103450420237,"c":1,"t":"self-discovery.","x":0.08626268795195155,"y":0.31123307210264461,"w":0.11987592061360677},{"t":"Each definition is slightly different - and tends to reflect the field of endeavour of each pioneer. It","x":0.088477375492942462,"h":0.015988372380376759,"w":0.77777776082356775,"y":0.34302325564605196,"c":1},{"w":0.76543207804361979,"y":0.36042402838229814,"c":1,"h":0.016029460129664885,"t":"was the same whoever I asked: the prominent historian would say exploration was a thing of the","x":0.088477376586655693},{"t":"past, the cutting-edge scientist would say it was of the present. And so on. They each set their own","h":0.020794063069373925,"c":1,"y":0.37475720060468776,"x":0.08834081972955507,"w":0.78213699340820297},{"x":0.088477366467402591,"y":0.39389534869125487,"t":"particular criteria; the common factor in their approach being that they all had, unlike many of us","h":0.015998644317698929,"c":1,"w":0.77572016398111987},{"c":1,"t":"who simply enjoy travel or discovering new things, both a very definite objective from the outset","w":0.77160491943359377,"x":0.088477375572618186,"y":0.41133720915602778,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"w":0.33156059265136717,"y":0.42693663125395043,"x":0.086297085955387348,"t":"and also a desire to record their findings.","h":0.01654590229263575,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.74279836018880219,"y":0.46075581380741082,"t":"I'd best declare my own bias. As a writer, I'm interested in the exploration of ideas. I've done","x":0.088477363011976895},{"h":0.017447792879965118,"x":0.088403636050016041,"y":0.47648100725538833,"t":"a great many expeditions and each one was unique. I've lived for months alone with isolated","w":0.73678685506184904,"c":1},{"x":0.088477362186764788,"c":1,"t":"groups of people all around the world, even two 'uncontacted tribes'. But none of these things","h":0.017667844522968212,"y":0.49263839807812615,"w":0.74897120157877595},{"y":0.51015041634525482,"c":1,"h":0.018134509155129708,"w":0.75935811360677086,"t":"is of the slightest interest to anyone unless, through my books, I've found a new slant, explored","x":0.088432039182392827},{"t":"a new idea. Why? Because the world has moved on. The time has long passed for the great","x":0.090534970837940043,"y":0.52761627893652852,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"w":0.72222223917643225},{"x":0.088477364900329578,"t":"continental voyages - another walk to the poles, another crossing of the Empty Quarter. We","y":0.5450530037010175,"w":0.73045267740885422,"c":1,"h":0.015993508068214979},{"t":"know how the land surface of our planet lies; exploration of it is now down to the details - the","w":0.75118876139322921,"h":0.019786845949709919,"y":0.55993717888924854,"c":1,"x":0.0884077645998326},{"y":0.57703488356135124,"w":0.74897120157877606,"x":0.088477362080412542,"h":0.017488084777364743,"c":1,"t":"habits of microbes, say, or the grazing behaviour of buffalo. Aside from the deep sea and deep"},{"c":1,"x":0.088477375571269001,"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.77160491943359388,"t":"underground, it's the era of specialists. However, this is to disregard the role the human mind has","y":0.59447674404010498},{"x":0.088477378703300733,"y":0.61042402836324472,"c":1,"w":0.75308639526367183,"h":0.017482948527880904,"t":"in conveying remote places; and this is what interests me: how a fresh interpretation, even of a"},{"h":0.017667844522968212,"w":0.43209874471028648,"t":"well-travelled route, can give its readers new insights.","c":1,"x":0.088477376502013858,"y":0.62779740850189869},{"x":0.84567901186996264,"c":1,"y":0.91860465098577604,"w":0.026748971939086985,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"25"}],"h":3395}